<div><p class="tb-ey">Tool two</p><h2 class="rv">Moon phase calculator</h2><p class="tb-p">A moon phase display follows the 29.53-day lunar cycle. Choose any date to see the moon as your watch should show it, and how a moon phase watch keeps up over time.</p>
<label class="tb-lb" for="mn-d">Date</label><input type="date" id="mn-d" class="tb-date"><dl class="tb-read" aria-live="polite"><div><dt>Illuminated</dt><dd id="mn-i">0%</dd></div><div><dt>Next full moon</dt><dd id="mn-f">&ndash;</dd></div><div><dt>Next new moon</dt><dd id="mn-nw">&ndash;</dd></div></dl>
<div class="tb-drift"><p><b>Standard moon phase:</b> a 59-tooth disc is off by one day after about <b>2.5 years</b>.</p><p><b>High-precision:</b> a 135-tooth disc stays within a day for about <b>122 years</b>.</p></div><figure class="tb-mn-i rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1770591482123-3926a64328bb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=600&h=240&q=75" alt="a full moon glowing in the night sky" width="600" height="240" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div></section>

<section class="tb-s tb-tc"><div class="tb-w tb-tc-g"><div><p class="tb-ey">Inside a tourbillon</p><h2 class="rv">A whirlwind in a cage</h2><p class="tb-p">In 1801 Abraham-Louis Breguet patented a way to cancel out gravity&rsquo;s small, steady pull on a pocket watch&rsquo;s balance. He put the whole escapement in a cage that turns, usually once a minute.</p><ol class="tb-parts"><li class="rv"><span>01</span><div><b>Fixed fourth wheel</b><p>Bolted to the movement. The cage&rsquo;s pinion rolls around it.</p></div></li><li class="rv"><span>02</span><div><b>Rotating cage</b><p>A light carriage, often under half a gram, turning once a minute.</p></div></li><li class="rv"><span>03</span><div><b>Escapement</b><p>Escape wheel and pallet fork, riding inside the cage.</p></div></li><li class="rv"><span>04</span><div><b>Balance and hairspring</b><p>The regulator, carried round with the cage so gravity&rsquo;s pull averages out.</p></div></li></ol></div><div class="tb-tc-v"><svg class="tb-cage tb-cage-b" viewBox="0 0 200 200" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="100" cy="100" r="92" class="ring"/><g class="rot"><path d="M100 100L100.0 184.0" /><path d="M100 100L27.3 58.0" /><path d="M100 100L172.7 58.0" /><circle cx="100" cy="100" r="84" class="frame"/><g class="bal"><circle cx="100" cy="100" r="40" class="wheel"/><path d="M60 100h80M100 60v80" class="sp"/></g><circle cx="100" cy="100" r="6" class="jw"/><circle cx="100" cy="16" r="5" class="jw"/></g></svg><p>One full turn every 60 seconds</p></div></div></section>

<section class="tb-s tb-hs"><div class="tb-w tb-sh tb-sh-c"><p class="tb-ey">A short history</p><h2 class="rv">From shadow to wrist</h2></div><div class="tb-w"><ol class="tb-time"><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1778986772559-f6c4997139d5?auto=format&fit=crop&w=360&h=360&q=75" alt="a weathered sundial in a garden" width="360" height="360" loading="lazy"></figure><span>c. 1500 BC</span><b>Sundial</b><p>Time read from the sun&rsquo;s shadow.</p></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1787752040058-611052b7d197?auto=format&fit=crop&w=360&h=360&q=75" alt="a brass hourglass with white sand" width="360" height="360" loading="lazy"></figure><span>c. 1300</span><b>Hourglass</b><p>Sand measures a fixed span, day or night.</p></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1747466403454-d0518287e433?auto=format&fit=crop&w=360&h=360&q=75" alt="the astronomical clock in Prague's old town square" width="360" height="360" loading="lazy"></figure><span>1410</span><b>Astronomical clock</b><p>Gears track the sun, moon and stars.</p></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1791703901480-0a770a813293?auto=format&fit=crop&w=360&h=360&q=75" alt="an open silver pocket watch with its chain" width="360" height="360" loading="lazy"></figure><span>1700s</span><b>Pocket watch</b><p>A personal clock, carried on a chain.</p></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1774744287122-4a0c96786dbd?auto=format&fit=crop&w=360&h=360&q=75" alt="a stainless steel wristwatch in close up" width="360" height="360" loading="lazy"></figure><span>1900s</span><b>Wristwatch</b><p>Time on the wrist, built for everyday life.</p></li></ol></div></section>

